WEBVTT

00:21.720 --> 00:23.910
Yuko, it's me.

00:23.910 --> 00:26.170
What is it, Himura-senpai?

00:26.590 --> 00:28.630
Let's leave this town together.

00:28.850 --> 00:32.480
I can't leave you in a place like that for another second!

00:32.480 --> 00:34.130
Selfish words, don't you think?

00:34.410 --> 00:37.140
We'll make a fresh start far away from that man.

00:37.670 --> 00:39.100
Won't you come with me?

00:45.070 --> 00:46.870
Come with me.

00:46.870 --> 00:48.770
How forceful...

00:49.160 --> 00:52.030
Okay, if you say so.

00:52.680 --> 00:55.700
Love, I've got to feel it

00:55.980 --> 00:59.030
If you put your trust in me

00:59.300 --> 01:02.550
I know what my life would be

01:02.620 --> 01:07.440
Oh, you are all I ever need

01:07.600 --> 01:13.140
I try to hear what you say

01:13.290 --> 01:15.410
So I pray

01:15.490 --> 01:18.990
But you're fading away

01:20.430 --> 01:26.150
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:26.580 --> 01:29.780
We won't fall apart

01:29.900 --> 01:37.960
'Cause you're my only star

01:39.920 --> 01:43.670
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:43.670 --> 01:47.180
Calling you, so like a little child

01:47.340 --> 01:50.420
All the things you have in mind

01:50.680 --> 01:53.800
I wish I could see your insides

01:53.800 --> 01:56.830
My love, you've got to feel it

01:56.830 --> 02:00.140
And if we put our trust in you and me

02:00.350 --> 02:03.800
You know what our lives would be

02:03.920 --> 02:11.760
Oh, you are the one, I believe

02:22.410 --> 02:24.330
Kuze! Kuze!

02:28.160 --> 02:29.830
Kuze, are you all right?

02:30.170 --> 02:31.170
You're alive, right?

02:31.830 --> 02:36.670
I think it would be better to be in hell than to see your faces right after waking up.

02:36.670 --> 02:38.420
Should I call 119?

02:38.420 --> 02:39.930
000 is fine.

02:40.720 --> 02:43.430
It's all right. I don't need an ambulance.

02:43.760 --> 02:46.770
I settled everything with Mizuki-chan a little while ago.

02:47.310 --> 02:50.810
The way we parted makes it impossible for us to ever meet again.

02:50.810 --> 02:53.230
Just like with my ex-girlfriend.

02:53.230 --> 02:54.270
You jackass!

02:55.610 --> 02:57.570
Didn't you want to experience youth?

02:57.570 --> 02:59.820
Don't you think we're too old for that?

02:59.820 --> 03:01.360
Settling matters is fine,

03:01.360 --> 03:04.330
but if you don't slow down, even your treasured memories will disappear.

03:05.410 --> 03:08.120
I won't be troubled if I lose any of my memories.

03:08.120 --> 03:10.330
You've had happy experiences, haven't you?

03:10.330 --> 03:11.710
Have you?

03:12.290 --> 03:13.710
Who knows?

03:13.710 --> 03:14.840
I don't remember.

03:21.720 --> 03:23.840
The weather is really nice here.

03:24.260 --> 03:26.430
Since we've come such a long way.

03:26.930 --> 03:29.310
Now, what should we do next?

03:29.310 --> 03:31.850
You didn't plan this at all?

03:31.850 --> 03:33.940
I guess we'll start by getting something to eat.

03:36.150 --> 03:39.900
Anyway, let's visit some real estate agents and find a place to live.

03:39.900 --> 03:42.570
And then I'll find a job.

03:42.570 --> 03:43.410
What's wrong?

03:43.410 --> 03:44.620
You're not going to eat?

03:44.620 --> 03:47.660
Didn't you say that you don't eat lunch?

03:47.660 --> 03:50.910
I don't have a reason to obey that rule anymore.

03:50.910 --> 03:53.170
Is this really okay with you?

03:53.170 --> 03:54.710
Is what okay?

03:54.710 --> 03:56.920
Didn't you say that you were aiming for the top?

03:58.460 --> 04:00.920
I've forgotten about that already.

04:01.670 --> 04:07.100
It's pointless to run off with someone like me and throw your life away.

04:07.100 --> 04:08.640
Really?

04:08.640 --> 04:11.980
You'll regret doing something like this.

04:11.980 --> 04:13.190
I already have.

04:14.270 --> 04:18.480
From now on, I won't have any more regrets.

04:18.480 --> 04:22.450
You said I was your first love, right?

04:22.450 --> 04:23.780
Yes.

04:23.780 --> 04:26.910
You also said your first love hasn't ended yet, right?

04:26.910 --> 04:27.700
Yes.

04:28.330 --> 04:29.580
Is that still true?

04:30.740 --> 04:31.750
All right, old man.

04:31.750 --> 04:32.580
Thanks for the meal.

04:31.750 --> 04:32.580
What's wrong?

04:32.580 --> 04:34.330
You usually answer right away, don't you?

04:32.580 --> 04:33.290
Come again!

04:33.290 --> 04:34.330
Hot!

04:35.540 --> 04:39.090
It's true that I love you,

04:39.090 --> 04:41.840
and my feelings haven't changed.

04:42.090 --> 04:43.840
It's not a lie. I'm telling the truth.

04:46.430 --> 04:47.340
Yuko.

04:48.220 --> 04:49.100
Yes.

04:50.470 --> 04:54.730
It really is tiring not to blink.

04:54.980 --> 04:55.940
Gosh...

04:55.940 --> 04:58.230
Gosh, don't you just get tired of it?

05:00.730 --> 05:03.190
Damn it! What was that about?!

05:03.190 --> 05:05.110
It's no use, Senpai.

05:05.110 --> 05:08.490
Unless we tell them our situation clearly, no one's going to rent us a room.

05:08.490 --> 05:10.830
Didn't I tell them enough?

05:10.830 --> 05:12.790
We're two students who've run away from home, right?

05:13.000 --> 05:15.500
That's certainly enough for people to doubt us.

05:15.750 --> 05:17.370
We're in a tight spot.

05:17.370 --> 05:21.130
We won't have anywhere to stay tonight unless we find a room.

05:21.130 --> 05:23.380
Unexpectedly, you don't know how to make a plan.

05:23.380 --> 05:26.380
How could I make a plan for such an irregular situation?

05:26.380 --> 05:28.050
I guess it can't be helped.

05:28.050 --> 05:31.260
How about we find a hotel to stay in tonight?

05:31.260 --> 05:32.220
Hotel?

05:32.220 --> 05:35.600
Senpai, you just thought of something dirty, didn't you?

05:35.600 --> 05:38.100
O-Of course not!

05:38.100 --> 05:39.730
Stop that nonsense!

05:41.650 --> 05:43.650
I guess you're right.

05:44.610 --> 05:46.780
There's no way you would, is there?

05:51.910 --> 05:54.250
We'll visit another one.

05:54.250 --> 05:55.290
Okay!

06:03.880 --> 06:05.340
That was too bad.

06:05.710 --> 06:06.720
Yeah...

06:06.920 --> 06:09.090
We'll definitely find one tomorrow.

06:09.430 --> 06:10.510
Yeah...

06:11.100 --> 06:13.510
Aren't we going to stay at a hotel?

06:16.100 --> 06:17.600
I see.

06:17.600 --> 06:21.270
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it like that.

06:21.270 --> 06:24.780
I just want to be frugal with our savings until I find a job.

06:25.610 --> 06:29.200
Since I can't look for a job until we have an address.

06:29.200 --> 06:30.570
You're right.

06:38.040 --> 06:39.830
Weren't you a Christian?

06:39.830 --> 06:41.830
Well, they're all gods too.

06:42.290 --> 06:44.460
I don't understand you at all.

06:45.090 --> 06:48.090
Thank you for letting us stay here tonight.

06:48.880 --> 06:50.590
Good thing it's summer.

06:51.260 --> 06:53.600
We'd freeze to death if it were winter.

06:53.600 --> 06:55.890
It gets cold at night even in the summer, too.

06:57.060 --> 07:00.270
But if we're like this, we'll be warm.

07:04.770 --> 07:06.030
You don't mind?

07:06.030 --> 07:07.610
About what?

07:07.610 --> 07:11.320
I'm damaged.

07:11.320 --> 07:14.950
That doesn't change the fact that you're Yuko.

07:15.450 --> 07:20.080
My feelings for you won't change, regardless of your condition.

07:20.540 --> 07:21.750
Senpai...

07:31.380 --> 07:32.840
The building is twenty years old,

07:32.840 --> 07:34.800
and our place is just one room with four and a half mats.

07:35.180 --> 07:37.470
The kitchen and toilet are shared.

07:37.470 --> 07:40.810
Despite these conditions, the rent is more expensive than my old place.

07:41.640 --> 07:45.360
But there's no security deposit or advance, and we can move in here right away.

07:45.360 --> 07:48.820
And they rented us this place even after that inadequate explanation of our situation.

07:48.820 --> 07:51.400
We should feel lucky to find this place.

07:51.400 --> 07:54.660
So I guess this apartment is for people who have their reasons.

07:54.660 --> 07:56.450
We should be careful about security.

07:57.030 --> 08:01.210
Is there anything worth stealing from people who don't even have cell phones?

08:01.540 --> 08:03.330
I guess you're right.

08:03.330 --> 08:04.830
What is that?

08:09.510 --> 08:10.840
It's a memento of Akane.

08:11.380 --> 08:14.340
A red wristwatch I bought her for Christmas.

08:15.220 --> 08:18.350
That's your deceased younger sister's...

08:18.930 --> 08:21.350
This is the one thing I couldn't leave behind.

08:24.190 --> 08:26.110
Your sketchbook...

08:26.110 --> 08:29.360
I thought I might be able to use this to kill time.

08:29.650 --> 08:31.280
That's...

08:31.280 --> 08:34.610
Yeah, the one you threw at me.

08:34.610 --> 08:35.700
Senpai...

08:37.160 --> 08:38.530
Could it be...

08:38.530 --> 08:39.700
because of that...

08:42.710 --> 08:44.120
I'm going home.

08:44.120 --> 08:44.960
Yuko!

08:45.330 --> 08:47.880
Is this sympathy? Are you pitying me?

08:48.090 --> 08:50.460
I don't want things like that!

08:50.460 --> 08:51.800
Wait, Yuko!

08:51.800 --> 08:54.840
I didn't come all this way for that!

08:55.880 --> 08:57.430
Yuko!

09:09.480 --> 09:10.520
Yuko...

09:11.480 --> 09:13.110
Please wait, Yuko!

09:13.110 --> 09:14.700
Please let go!

09:14.700 --> 09:15.950
Calm down!

09:22.290 --> 09:24.830
I was an idiot for ever believing you at all.

09:28.630 --> 09:33.840
In the end, you also see me as just a tool for self-satisfaction, don't you?

09:34.210 --> 09:37.010
You probably don't even care how I feel.

09:37.010 --> 09:39.090
You're no different from Akira-nii-san!

09:49.020 --> 09:50.270
I'm sorry.

09:51.020 --> 09:54.650
Yuko, you might be correct.

09:55.320 --> 09:58.820
I'm the same as Amamiya.

09:58.820 --> 10:03.620
I've always regretted that I couldn't protect Akane.

10:04.200 --> 10:09.540
But this is neither sympathy nor pity.

10:09.540 --> 10:11.880
You aren't my replacement for Akane, either!

10:12.630 --> 10:13.710
I...

10:13.710 --> 10:16.220
Yuko, I want to protect you!

10:17.130 --> 10:18.720
Senpai...

10:20.050 --> 10:23.010
I'll never let go of these hands again!

10:28.020 --> 10:31.520
Down from the sky

10:28.020 --> 10:31.520
One white feather is floating, wavering

10:34.400 --> 10:35.610
I'm home.

10:35.860 --> 10:38.240
Welcome back, Yu-kun.

10:38.240 --> 10:40.070
How was your job?

10:40.070 --> 10:41.660
I'm still in training.

10:41.660 --> 10:43.410
Technically, it's not really a job yet.

10:43.410 --> 10:45.120
Dinner is ready.

10:45.120 --> 10:47.120
Please eat while it's hot.

10:47.120 --> 10:47.960
Yeah.

10:48.830 --> 10:50.920
It feels kind of nice.

10:50.920 --> 10:52.290
What does?

10:52.290 --> 10:53.920
The lights are on.

10:53.920 --> 10:55.500
Of course.

10:55.500 --> 10:58.630
No matter how poor we are, we can at least turn the lights on.

10:58.630 --> 10:59.880
That's not what I meant.

11:00.380 --> 11:04.350
When I lived by myself, the lights were never on when I came home.

11:06.430 --> 11:09.640
It feels nice to come home to a place where someone is waiting for me.

11:09.640 --> 11:10.940
Is that so?

11:10.940 --> 11:14.770
But I'll turn off the lights if you come home late.

11:14.770 --> 11:16.900
And then I'll sleep with the door locked.

11:16.900 --> 11:17.440
Hey...

11:17.440 --> 11:19.440
Even if you cry and beg, I won't let you in.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.700
Hey, hey!

11:21.700 --> 11:24.780
So please come home early, all right?

11:25.160 --> 11:30.790
Because the place you call home is my home as well.

11:31.210 --> 11:35.340
This place is my home, too.

11:36.170 --> 11:37.050
Yeah.

11:42.800 --> 11:45.350
Was it really all right?

11:45.550 --> 11:46.930
About what?

11:46.930 --> 11:49.350
I'm just a burden.

11:49.350 --> 11:50.600
Why...

11:51.020 --> 11:56.900
You're throwing away everything you've worked so hard for.

11:56.900 --> 11:59.440
I just have to work hard again, that's all.

11:59.440 --> 12:00.610
Yu-kun...

12:01.030 --> 12:04.110
Let's start fresh from here.

12:04.110 --> 12:05.450
Yu-kun...

12:05.450 --> 12:06.370
What is it?

12:06.780 --> 12:08.870
Please draw me.

12:09.240 --> 12:10.370
Yuko?

12:12.620 --> 12:16.880
I'm not very good at portraits, but I guess I'll give it a shot.

12:16.880 --> 12:17.750
Okay.

12:20.590 --> 12:23.430
When I told her about the time I broke up with my ex,

12:23.430 --> 12:26.430
she started crying in my stead,

12:27.100 --> 12:29.350
even though I hadn't cried.

12:30.020 --> 12:31.520
I wonder why.

12:31.520 --> 12:34.100
But I really feel like crying right now.

12:34.100 --> 12:35.520
Kuze...

12:35.520 --> 12:38.150
I've never failed in my life,

12:38.150 --> 12:42.360
but that's because I've run away from everything I might fail at.

12:42.780 --> 12:43.610
Even then...

12:43.740 --> 12:44.860
Even then!

12:44.860 --> 12:47.740
Why do I have to face a challenge I can't run away from?!

12:47.740 --> 12:50.490
Why do I have to accept a challenge I can't win?!

12:50.830 --> 12:51.830
Kuze...

12:52.040 --> 12:55.460
This heart, and Mizuki-chan too...

12:55.460 --> 12:59.250
I don't have a future left, so what am I supposed to do?

12:59.250 --> 13:02.130
What else can I do?!

13:02.130 --> 13:04.630
Kuze, I understand your feelings, but...

13:05.470 --> 13:07.260
There's no way you could understand!

13:07.260 --> 13:08.550
I'm broken!

13:08.890 --> 13:11.140
The two of you aren't, so how could you understand?!

13:11.140 --> 13:14.270
Even so, nothing good will come from despairing!

13:14.270 --> 13:17.400
I know I'm going to die soon, so of course nothing good will happen!

13:17.400 --> 13:19.980
If you give up from the start, nothing will ever happen.

13:22.070 --> 13:23.780
You're the last person I want to hear that from.

13:24.950 --> 13:28.820
You couldn't manage to give it up, and so you're still hanging onto something that ended long ago.

13:28.820 --> 13:30.330
What the hell would you know?

13:30.330 --> 13:31.370
Kuze!

13:32.490 --> 13:34.250
It still hasn't ended.

13:34.710 --> 13:36.160
You've got to be kidding me.

13:36.160 --> 13:37.710
It's not like you'll ever be able to see her again.

13:39.330 --> 13:44.210
You'll never be able to see Amamiya Yuko again.

13:49.140 --> 13:50.970
On your way home now?

13:53.100 --> 13:54.180
Amamiya...

13:54.520 --> 13:57.390
Do you make enough to support yourselves?

13:57.390 --> 13:59.810
It's hard for a dropout to find a job, isn't it?

13:59.810 --> 14:00.980
What are you here for?

14:01.400 --> 14:03.610
To buy some cigarettes.

14:03.610 --> 14:05.570
I'm not giving Yuko to you.

14:05.570 --> 14:07.860
That's not for you to decide.

14:07.860 --> 14:09.160
What?

14:09.160 --> 14:11.990
Of course, it's not something for me to decide either.

14:11.990 --> 14:14.750
Do you really think Yuko would go back to you?

14:15.200 --> 14:18.830
She might, if she has nowhere else to go.

14:18.830 --> 14:21.250
You can't provide a home for her.

14:21.250 --> 14:22.420
What?

14:24.170 --> 14:27.340
You're just an escape for her, not a real home,

14:28.300 --> 14:32.010
because you're running away as well.

14:32.010 --> 14:33.640
I'm not running away!

14:34.930 --> 14:37.640
You did though, didn't you? On the day of the earthquake.

14:38.940 --> 14:42.900
That's right. You abandoned your precious sister.

14:42.900 --> 14:47.900
Since then, you've avoided conflict and continued to run away.

14:47.900 --> 14:51.160
That's why you let go of Yuko's hands,

14:51.160 --> 14:54.240
and you gave up drawing and threw away your colors.

14:54.240 --> 14:56.290
You ran away from me.

14:56.290 --> 14:58.540
You threw away everything you'd worked for and ran away.

14:58.540 --> 14:59.500
No!

14:59.500 --> 15:00.870
It's not like that!

15:00.870 --> 15:02.880
Aren't you still trying to run?

15:03.170 --> 15:06.300
In the end, all you're doing is running away.

15:06.300 --> 15:09.260
Then what else could I have done?!

15:09.260 --> 15:11.380
You know that for yourself, don't you?

15:13.550 --> 15:14.890
You're too careless.

15:14.890 --> 15:17.100
Get a decent lock.

15:18.100 --> 15:24.860
What you could have done was die with your sister in that earthquake.

15:28.240 --> 15:29.690
I understand that very well,

15:29.690 --> 15:32.740
because I wanted to do the same myself.

15:32.740 --> 15:36.870
But on that day, I wasn't with my sister.

15:37.410 --> 15:40.160
I envy you,

15:40.160 --> 15:42.580
and at the same time, I despise you.

15:42.580 --> 15:45.630
You were with your sister on that day, weren't you?

15:45.960 --> 15:48.000
Yet you ran away.

15:51.130 --> 15:54.180
You didn't even help her, but ran away instead.

15:52.680 --> 15:54.180
YOU RAN AWAY

15:54.470 --> 15:57.560
You didn't die with your sister, but you ran away.

15:58.060 --> 16:01.310
She was so precious to you, but you ran away.

16:01.600 --> 16:05.190
She was calling out to you in pain and fear, but you ran away.

16:05.480 --> 16:08.820
You could have died with her, but you ran away.

16:09.320 --> 16:12.860
It was your destiny, but you ran away.

16:15.910 --> 16:19.120
Have you repented for your sins against her?

16:19.330 --> 16:22.540
Has she forgiven you?

16:22.540 --> 16:25.420
Are you in a position to desire happiness?

16:27.090 --> 16:30.340
You're running away again.

16:30.710 --> 16:32.840
And with that, you're going to lose something again.

16:33.380 --> 16:36.340
Even the place where you hope to return.

17:13.840 --> 17:16.590
I'm... going to lose him again.

17:22.390 --> 17:23.930
Am I running away?

17:24.600 --> 17:28.020
Am I... running away again?

17:31.110 --> 17:32.690
Yu-kun?

17:32.780 --> 17:33.650
Yu-kun!

17:34.240 --> 17:36.660
Yu-kun, where are you?

17:37.160 --> 17:39.240
Please come back, Senpai!

17:39.240 --> 17:41.120
Where did you go?

17:41.120 --> 17:43.410
Senpai! Himura-senpai!

17:44.000 --> 17:45.290
Where are you, Senpai?

17:45.290 --> 17:46.540
Where are you?

17:46.960 --> 17:48.750
Senpai...

17:48.750 --> 17:50.170
Onii-chan!

17:50.460 --> 17:52.340
Onii-chan!

17:52.340 --> 17:54.800
Where are you, Senpai?

17:55.420 --> 17:58.180
Onii-chan!

18:09.060 --> 18:11.060
Onii-chan...

18:12.360 --> 18:13.530
Welcome back.

18:16.990 --> 18:18.240
Shall we go home?

18:54.190 --> 19:03.370
motomeai sakenderu

18:54.190 --> 19:03.370
We long for each other and cry aloud.

19:04.910 --> 19:14.210
negai no kakera dakishimeru

19:04.910 --> 19:14.210
I embrace the fragment of a wish.

19:15.590 --> 19:24.850
yume wo mite mezametemo

19:15.590 --> 19:24.850
Even after awakening from a dream

19:26.220 --> 19:38.190
kienai ai wo ima utau

19:26.220 --> 19:38.190
I sing for everlasting love.

20:10.430 --> 20:14.980
Save me

20:14.980 --> 20:15.060
Save me

20:29.160 --> 20:30.540
Yu!

20:30.540 --> 20:32.540
Didn't you want to experience youth?

20:32.540 --> 20:33.540
Are you satisfied now?

20:34.870 --> 20:38.920
You'll never be able to see Amamiya Yuko again.

20:38.920 --> 20:39.840
Kuze!

20:39.840 --> 20:43.380
I won't be able to die in peace if I don't say it.

20:43.380 --> 20:46.850
Yu, you're the one who needs to be told to give up on it.

20:46.850 --> 20:48.100
Settle it already.

20:55.190 --> 20:58.730
Kuze, there are things you can and can't say.

20:59.650 --> 21:01.230
Oh, really?

21:01.230 --> 21:05.240
You say that, but you're still hanging on to him too, aren't you?

21:08.320 --> 21:10.030
Calm down.

21:12.120 --> 21:14.120
Me

21:15.250 --> 21:17.920
Why do you exist?

21:20.880 --> 21:23.970
I haven't had that dream for a long time.

21:26.340 --> 21:29.010
Mizuki-chan, there's a delivery for you.

21:29.390 --> 21:31.220
For me?

21:32.310 --> 21:34.230
This is Kuze-san's...

21:34.480 --> 21:36.900
The delivery person must've made a mistake.

21:36.900 --> 21:41.230
But this is the right address, and you're the recipient.

21:48.530 --> 21:53.450
So I guess the one that was broken was Kuze-san...

21:48.700 --> 21:50.240
So what was broken is...

21:50.240 --> 21:53.450
Sorry

21:50.240 --> 21:53.450
Farewell

21:53.450 --> 21:55.460
Memory

22:13.220 --> 22:15.930
It's bad for a violin to come in contact with salty air.

22:16.270 --> 22:17.770
Nagi-san...

22:17.770 --> 22:19.600
The same goes for tears, too.

22:21.310 --> 22:23.860
I was really surprised that time,

22:23.860 --> 22:26.860
because you told me you were his girlfriend.

22:26.860 --> 22:28.570
Even if two people are separated physically,

22:28.570 --> 22:32.580
as long as they have feelings for each other, it's not really over.

22:32.580 --> 22:34.870
Not over, huh...

22:34.870 --> 22:38.000
"In love, you lose if you fall for the other person.

22:38.000 --> 22:39.750
You're supposed to make the other person fall in love with you."

22:41.460 --> 22:43.290
Kuze used to always say that.

22:44.420 --> 22:46.670
That sounds like Kuze-san, all right.

22:46.670 --> 22:48.130
But this time,

22:48.130 --> 22:51.550
although you fell for him, it looks like Kuze is the one who lost.

22:51.550 --> 22:53.180
That's not true...

22:53.180 --> 22:56.140
I'm the one who's been defeated.

22:56.390 --> 22:58.560
Geez, I just want to cry.

22:58.560 --> 22:59.640
But...

23:01.100 --> 23:02.560
you aren't running away.

23:06.820 --> 23:09.990
He only participates in things he can win,

23:09.990 --> 23:13.320
so he can't win against people who come back for more even after losing.

23:17.910 --> 23:19.750
It seems like the only one who can save him now...

23:20.290 --> 23:22.420
is you.

23:25.670 --> 23:30.380
A sudden twist of fate causes hearts to shatter.

23:30.380 --> 23:33.470
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.470 --> 23:34.890
Return.

23:35.510 --> 23:38.560
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
